Subject: Disable embedded GDB script assembly for Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Applies-After: ports/patch/boost-filc.patch

Use Boost's existing opt-out in the compiler configuration so it also applies
to installed header consumers. JSON and Unordered otherwise emit .pushsection
module assembly, rejected by Fil-C. This only removes embedded debugger scripts.

--- a/boost/config/compiler/clang.hpp
+++ b/boost/config/compiler/clang.hpp
@@ -9,6 +9,11 @@
 // Clang compiler setup.
 
 #define BOOST_HAS_PRAGMA_ONCE
+
+// Fil-C does not accept the module assembly used to embed debugger scripts.
+#if defined(__FILC__) && !defined(BOOST_ALL_NO_EMBEDDED_GDB_SCRIPTS)
+#  define BOOST_ALL_NO_EMBEDDED_GDB_SCRIPTS
+#endif
 
 // Detecting `-fms-extension` compiler flag assuming that _MSC_VER defined when that flag is used.
 #if defined (_MSC_VER) && (__clang_major__ > 3 || (__clang_major__ == 3 && __clang_minor__ >= 4))
